1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:02,040
(All characters, places,
and organizations are fictional.)

2
00:00:02,040 --> 00:00:03,310
(Children and teens were filmed
under production guidelines.)

3
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:05,640
I'm talking about your mother.

4
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:07,880
She may have cast you and me out,

5
00:00:08,050 --> 00:00:10,050
but she will take our Ye Ri in.

6
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:13,790
Ye Ri has every right
to inherit your mother's fortune.

7
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:16,420
- What?
- Am I wrong?

8
00:00:16,920 --> 00:00:20,020
Ye Ri is your mother's
biological granddaughter.

9
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:21,160
She's flesh and blood.

10
00:00:21,290 --> 00:00:23,600
The very day
after Mother kicked me out...

11
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:25,230
and severed ties with me,

12
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:29,930
she transferred the restaurant
and the house to my ex-wife.

13
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,200
She has nothing left.

14
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:34,840
It's all in my ex-wife's name.

15
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:38,840
I overheard the neighborhood women
and grandmas...

16
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:41,310
talking about your mother
at the clinic desk.

17
00:00:41,550 --> 00:00:44,180
She just keeps it quiet,
but they say she's secretly loaded.

18
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:46,450
Really?

19
00:00:47,790 --> 00:00:49,290
Are people in the neighborhood
really saying that?

20
00:00:50,220 --> 00:00:54,790
- I doubt it.
- Then bet your taxi on it.

21
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:57,730
I'm willing to bet my couch
that she's loaded.

22
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,770
Can't you return them?
Should I go instead?

23
00:01:00,970 --> 00:01:02,130
No, I'll just go.

24
00:01:03,230 --> 00:01:06,270
Just please go to work
quietly, okay?

25
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:09,270
Good grief...

26
00:01:11,380 --> 00:01:14,380
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

27
00:01:15,310 --> 00:01:16,880
Come pick up the shoes?

28
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:21,220
Did he come into work early
just to return the shoes?

29
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:28,530
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

30
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:39,970
Doesn't look like Mi Mi is out here.

31
00:01:44,140 --> 00:01:46,510
What am I even supposed to say
when I return these?

32
00:01:48,680 --> 00:01:50,450
These are famous play scripts.

33
00:01:51,450 --> 00:01:56,220
I've been wanting to reread them.
Are you giving these to me too?

34
00:01:57,690 --> 00:01:59,220
I knew you would like them.

35
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:01,230
I'm glad I kept them
on my bookshelf.

36
00:02:02,630 --> 00:02:04,960
First the shoes, now these books...

37
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:07,100
I'm not sure if it's okay...

38
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,770
to keep taking things
from you like this.

39
00:02:09,170 --> 00:02:12,140
I should find a way to repay you.

40
00:02:12,140 --> 00:02:13,170
A colleague of mine...

41
00:02:13,170 --> 00:02:16,470
often gives me theater tickets.
Let's keep going together.

42
00:02:16,980 --> 00:02:20,110
As companions who share
a love for theater, that is.

43
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:23,310
I'd love to,

44
00:02:23,850 --> 00:02:27,520
but an owner can't keep abandoning
her restaurant.

45
00:02:28,290 --> 00:02:30,360
Yesterday was the first time
I stepped away,

46
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:32,390
and my family
was frantically looking for me.

47
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:38,800
I've been debating whether
to say this since yesterday.

48
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:42,230
- What is it?
- That outfit looks great on you.

49
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:46,970
You're teasing me because...

50
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:48,570
I've worn it
two days in a row, right?

51
00:02:49,570 --> 00:02:52,010
No, not at all.
It's nothing like that, I mean it.

52
00:02:52,410 --> 00:02:53,980
I plan to wear it to death.

53
00:02:54,280 --> 00:02:55,950
It's been a while since I spent
good money on something.

54
00:02:58,320 --> 00:02:59,780
Still, you should be careful.

55
00:03:00,650 --> 00:03:03,660
- Why?
- You're so pretty,

56
00:03:03,720 --> 00:03:05,790
so strange men might hit on you.

57
00:03:06,260 --> 00:03:07,260
Pardon?

58
00:03:09,630 --> 00:03:12,330
You sure know how to flatter people.

59
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:16,730
No, I am not just flattering you.
It could really happen.

60
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:20,770
Stop it. Not at my age.

61
00:03:21,710 --> 00:03:23,210
I mean it.

62
00:03:23,640 --> 00:03:26,680
Just in case,
let me show you something.

63
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:28,810
In a dangerous world like this,

64
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:31,580
there is a move every pretty woman
needs to know.

65
00:03:31,650 --> 00:03:32,650
Make sure you remember it.

66
00:03:33,620 --> 00:03:34,750
What move?

67
00:03:38,090 --> 00:03:39,360
One, two.

68
00:03:43,060 --> 00:03:44,930
Like this, give it a try.

69
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:47,730
Me? Right here?

70
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:51,000
Yes. First, clench your fists
tight like this.

71
00:03:51,640 --> 00:03:52,740
One, two.

72
00:03:58,040 --> 00:03:59,040
Like this?

73
00:03:59,810 --> 00:04:01,980
- One, two.
- Yes.

74
00:04:02,050 --> 00:04:04,280
Imagine running
into your worst enemy...

75
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,620
on a narrow bridge,

76
00:04:06,220 --> 00:04:09,590
and channel all your rage
into an uppercut.

77
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:14,160
Like this?

78
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:20,100
I had no idea,

79
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:23,900
- but you are pretty funny.
- It depends on who I am with...

80
00:04:23,970 --> 00:04:25,400
and what the situation is.

81
00:04:25,570 --> 00:04:28,470
Keep practicing, okay?

82
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:34,350
Thanks.

83
00:04:39,220 --> 00:04:40,650
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

84
00:04:40,790 --> 00:04:41,990
One, two.

85
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:43,090
One, two.

86
00:04:45,490 --> 00:04:47,060
(Ju Kyung Ho Internal Medicine)

87
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:48,730
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

88
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:50,560
I told you not to come,
but here you are.

89
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,360
Honey.

90
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:56,400
That dress looks nice on you.

91
00:04:56,970 --> 00:04:57,970
You look great.

92
00:05:02,270 --> 00:05:04,240
The reason I came today is, honey...

93
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,310
"Honey?"

94
00:05:06,310 --> 00:05:07,580
Since when am I your honey?

95
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:10,820
Do you think I bought and wore this
just to look good for you?

96
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,850
No, I just...

97
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,390
That is not what I mean...

98
00:05:20,990 --> 00:05:25,560
- Goodness, what on earth is...
- What is the matter, Mrs. Choi?

99
00:05:27,370 --> 00:05:29,100
Oh my goodness. Mi Mi.

100
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:33,640
Oh my goodness.

101
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:36,440
- Mi Mi.
- Hak Sung.

102
00:05:36,510 --> 00:05:37,610
Oh, no.

103
00:05:37,610 --> 00:05:38,640
Mom.

104
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:40,240
Mom.

105
00:05:40,810 --> 00:05:43,050
- You are bleeding.
- Bleeding?

106
00:05:43,110 --> 00:05:44,180
- Oh dear.
- I'm bleeding!

107
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:46,350
First thing in the morning,
and there is blood.

108
00:05:46,420 --> 00:05:48,120
Tell me about it.

109
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:51,720
Blood...

110
00:05:52,660 --> 00:05:53,660
(Pocket Tissues)

111
00:05:58,130 --> 00:05:59,200
I am sorry, Mom.

112
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:00,900
Even after I was told
not to come here.

113
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:03,370
- I am sorry.
- Do not just wipe it.

114
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:05,200
Roll it up and plug your nose,
you fool.

115
00:06:05,270 --> 00:06:06,270
Should I?

116
00:06:06,340 --> 00:06:08,570
Cross paths twice,
and there will be a funeral.

117
00:06:09,740 --> 00:06:12,540
Consider the bloody nose
your admission fee, and tell me,

118
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,250
why did you come back?

119
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:17,450
Well, there is something
I need to tell you.

120
00:06:18,150 --> 00:06:19,150
To me?

121
00:06:20,350 --> 00:06:21,820
Yes, just for a moment...

122
00:06:22,490 --> 00:06:24,190
Could we talk in private
for a second?

123
00:06:25,020 --> 00:06:26,790
Follow me then.

124
00:06:27,430 --> 00:06:28,430
Mother.

125
00:06:29,290 --> 00:06:30,330
Not at the house.

126
00:06:31,130 --> 00:06:34,530
We will give you two some space,
so talk here.

127
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:37,700
All right, let us do that then.

128
00:06:44,810 --> 00:06:46,440
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

129
00:06:50,550 --> 00:06:53,420
What is it? Make it quick and leave.

130
00:07:12,540 --> 00:07:13,570
Mi Mi.

131
00:07:14,610 --> 00:07:17,340
Hey, why are we leaving them alone?

132
00:07:17,740 --> 00:07:20,710
Is it really okay
to leave those two by themselves?

133
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,550
By the way,
you really packed a punch earlier.

134
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:27,750
Where did you learn that?
Just one powerful blow, all at once.

135
00:07:28,620 --> 00:07:30,960
You think this is funny?
Are you enjoying this?

136
00:07:32,020 --> 00:07:36,190
No, I am saying you did great.
It felt like ten years...

137
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:40,770
I mean 20 years of frustration
just washed right away.

138
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:42,900
By the way,

139
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:46,370
what do you think
he showed up to say?

140
00:07:46,670 --> 00:07:50,370
- Aren't you curious?
- No, I couldn't care less.

141
00:07:51,310 --> 00:07:53,080
Instead of those two, my daughter...

142
00:07:53,380 --> 00:07:54,380
I am far more worried
about the relationship...

143
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:55,380
between my daughter and me.

144
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:57,450
What about Da Mi?

145
00:07:58,050 --> 00:07:59,880
She is doing fine
at Mi Seon's place.

146
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:02,120
You don't remember
the hurtful things you said, do you?

147
00:08:02,620 --> 00:08:04,560
You made a mess
and took zero responsibility.

148
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:06,160
What did you just say?

149
00:08:06,260 --> 00:08:07,590
She is doing fine,
so everything is fine?

150
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:11,330
You may be my sister,

151
00:08:11,400 --> 00:08:12,760
but I really cannot
stand you lately.

152
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,770
Just so you know, okay?

153
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:28,380
Would my life be less exhausting
if Da Mi moved back in?

154
00:08:43,630 --> 00:08:47,500
Sweetheart. How is your new job?

155
00:08:47,930 --> 00:08:50,570
How are you finding the company?

156
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:54,810
Have you eaten?

157
00:08:55,340 --> 00:08:58,280
Do not skip meals
just because of work.

158
00:08:58,340 --> 00:08:59,740
(Sweetheart. How is your new job?
How are you finding the company?)

159
00:09:00,410 --> 00:09:02,280
(Have you eaten? Do not skip meals
just because of work.)

160
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:06,980
If anyone mistreats you
or acts mean,

161
00:09:07,620 --> 00:09:10,220
just quit and come home.
Do not put up with it.

162
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:13,860
I'm waiting for you.

163
00:09:15,090 --> 00:09:16,160
(If anyone mistreats you or acts mean,)

164
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:18,630
(just quit and come home.
Do not put up with it.)

165
00:09:30,880 --> 00:09:33,040
We are not moving after all.

166
00:09:33,680 --> 00:09:34,680
My wife...

167
00:09:35,010 --> 00:09:36,680
told me to give this back to you.

168
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:39,950
What? She said she won't take it?

169
00:09:40,850 --> 00:09:42,550
Yes. She said
that we have no right...

170
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:44,160
to accept the money
after everything that had happened.

171
00:09:44,760 --> 00:09:46,220
She cares about having nerve now?

172
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:49,360
Or does she have an ulterior motive?

173
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:52,130
Mother, that is not true at all.

174
00:09:52,400 --> 00:09:54,730
Good grief.

175
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:58,200
I never thought I would live to see
such a pathetic sight in my old age.

176
00:09:58,870 --> 00:10:00,070
Good grief.

177
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:03,610
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

178
00:10:07,880 --> 00:10:09,180
Is it still bleeding?

179
00:10:09,810 --> 00:10:13,250
No, it has pretty much stopped now.
Do not worry.

180
00:10:13,750 --> 00:10:15,250
It hasn't stopped.

181
00:10:18,720 --> 00:10:19,790
Take it back.

182
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:24,060
Keep it as an emergency fund
and use it when you are in a pinch.

183
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:27,430
No. I really cannot take it either.

184
00:10:29,530 --> 00:10:30,600
Well, Mom.

185
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:32,540
I will get going.

186
00:10:36,140 --> 00:10:37,380
Oh, dear.

187
00:10:38,380 --> 00:10:39,440
You pathetic fool.

188
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:44,380
Oh my goodness!

189
00:10:46,620 --> 00:10:49,490
Who does she think she is,
a street fighter?

190
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:57,960
I'm waiting for you.

191
00:11:01,130 --> 00:11:02,700
What are you smiling at?

192
00:11:04,970 --> 00:11:06,070
A text from Mom.

193
00:11:07,340 --> 00:11:10,540
- Is it good news?
- No.

194
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:14,110
She said if my boss abuses his power
or treats me poorly,

195
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:16,650
I should quit right away
and come home.

196
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:19,850
Am I not treating you
pretty well, though?

197
00:11:21,950 --> 00:11:23,390
Why are you not answering?

198
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:25,720
Well...

199
00:11:26,890 --> 00:11:30,630
I think I am not that bad.
I always make sure you are fed.

200
00:11:31,160 --> 00:11:32,760
You do make sure I eat.

201
00:11:33,060 --> 00:11:36,170
So are you saying
there is nothing else besides that?

202
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:42,170
Listen.

203
00:11:42,670 --> 00:11:44,640
Anyway, we are going to get busier.

204
00:11:44,710 --> 00:11:46,840
We will present
the 2027 spring and summer collection...

205
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,750
in front of the executives.
Would you take a look?

206
00:11:51,380 --> 00:11:54,350
- With the modified samples?
- Yes.

207
00:11:54,420 --> 00:11:55,990
From receiving the samples
to setting them up,

208
00:11:56,050 --> 00:11:57,490
make sure nothing is missing.

209
00:11:57,560 --> 00:11:59,490
The schedule and items
are all listed here.

210
00:11:59,790 --> 00:12:01,590
Yes, I will check them.

211
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:03,260
If there is anything
you do not understand,

212
00:12:03,330 --> 00:12:05,130
ask me one by one.

213
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:07,930
Do not just guess on your own
and handle things by yourself.

214
00:12:08,130 --> 00:12:09,130
Understood?

215
00:12:10,430 --> 00:12:12,570
Yes, I understand.

216
00:12:17,410 --> 00:12:19,510
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

217
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:31,190
(Hwanggeum Apparel 2027 Spring
and Summer Collection Presentation)

218
00:12:36,460 --> 00:12:39,000
Is this for Hwanggeum Apparel?
I will take it.

219
00:12:39,230 --> 00:12:41,100
- Your name?
- Kang Ye Ri.

220
00:12:43,870 --> 00:12:45,040
Here you go.

221
00:12:46,240 --> 00:12:47,270
Please sign here.

222
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:49,840
(Kang Ye Ri)

223
00:12:56,480 --> 00:12:57,580
You are Kang Da Mi, right?

224
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:01,190
I have a delivery for you.
I am in the lobby.

225
00:13:01,350 --> 00:13:03,290
- Where are you?
- Yes, I will be right down.

226
00:13:03,350 --> 00:13:04,660
Please wait a moment.

227
00:13:04,790 --> 00:13:07,420
I notified you in advance.
You should have been down here.

228
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,760
I have other stops to make.

229
00:13:11,830 --> 00:13:13,160
(Mailroom)

230
00:13:14,970 --> 00:13:16,700
There is a drop-off area
inside the lobby.

231
00:13:16,770 --> 00:13:19,370
- I will leave it here.
- Wait a minute, I am on my way...

232
00:13:19,370 --> 00:13:20,370
(Hwanggeum Apparel, Kang Da Mi)

233
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:22,040
It is not in front of the door,
but inside.

234
00:13:22,410 --> 00:13:24,810
If you look at the box,
your name is on it.

235
00:13:39,690 --> 00:13:40,720
Is it not here yet?

236
00:13:40,760 --> 00:13:41,830
Well...

237
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:44,760
I got a call saying it arrived,
but it was not in the lobby.

238
00:13:45,660 --> 00:13:47,260
Did you check who received it?

239
00:13:47,570 --> 00:13:50,630
The courier said he left it there.
I went down right away,

240
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:53,440
but where he said he left it,
no matter how much I searched...

241
00:13:54,070 --> 00:13:55,410
You did not receive it in person?

242
00:13:56,070 --> 00:13:58,480
He left it while I was heading down.

243
00:13:59,710 --> 00:14:01,250
Then you should have checked it
right away.

244
00:14:01,710 --> 00:14:03,050
Who he handed it to,

245
00:14:03,110 --> 00:14:05,220
where exactly he left it,
you should have verified that.

246
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:07,590
I checked every corner
of the first-floor lobby.

247
00:14:07,690 --> 00:14:09,250
Thinking someone else
took it by mistake,

248
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:12,020
- I even asked people directly.
- And did you find it?

249
00:14:12,890 --> 00:14:14,060
No.

250
00:14:30,310 --> 00:14:31,580
You're still not ready?

251
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,510
Some of the samples
are unaccounted for.

252
00:14:35,810 --> 00:14:36,950
I will check on it immediately.

253
00:14:39,050 --> 00:14:40,720
The executives are coming in soon.

254
00:14:41,420 --> 00:14:42,750
If things start like this
from our first review,

255
00:14:42,750 --> 00:14:44,460
it's going to be a problem,
Head Designer Cha.

256
00:14:47,160 --> 00:14:48,860
Who is managing the samples?

257
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:52,230
I was supposed to receive them.

258
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:54,300
And that's where
your responsibility ends?

259
00:14:55,430 --> 00:14:57,430
Do you know what we're doing
with those samples today?

260
00:14:57,900 --> 00:15:00,240
I'm sorry, ma'am.
I will go search again.

261
00:15:04,540 --> 00:15:05,610
Head Designer Cha.

262
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:08,110
Frankly, I'm disappointed.

263
00:15:09,380 --> 00:15:11,550
It isn't as if
you lacked time to prepare.

264
00:15:13,150 --> 00:15:14,620
I'll ensure everything proceeds
without issue.

265
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:16,250
I'm sorry.

266
00:15:37,710 --> 00:15:38,740
Kang Da Mi.

267
00:15:42,310 --> 00:15:43,880
If you couldn't find the samples,

268
00:15:43,950 --> 00:15:45,650
you should have contacted me
right then.

269
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,350
When you don't even know
where the delivered sample box is,

270
00:15:48,420 --> 00:15:50,190
how on earth are we supposed
to set things up?

271
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,190
I'm sorry.

272
00:15:54,090 --> 00:15:55,690
Everyone is waiting
for that package right now.

273
00:15:56,190 --> 00:15:58,530
If it hasn't arrived, say so.
If there's a problem, say so.

274
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:02,130
- Shouldn't you have told me?
- I thought that somehow...

275
00:16:02,130 --> 00:16:05,640
I could retrieve it on my own.
And I thought I had to.

276
00:16:06,170 --> 00:16:07,640
Haven't I told you time and again...

277
00:16:07,640 --> 00:16:08,870
never to make assumptions
on your own?

278
00:16:09,540 --> 00:16:10,740
Or you should have
found the samples...

279
00:16:10,740 --> 00:16:12,940
so that this whole mess
never happened in the first place.

280
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:18,420
We start at ten o'clock.

281
00:16:19,550 --> 00:16:20,550
Okay.

282
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:25,260
At this rate,

283
00:16:25,320 --> 00:16:27,260
the evaluation will turn
into a total disaster...

284
00:16:27,260 --> 00:16:28,290
before it even starts.

285
00:16:30,560 --> 00:16:31,600
Kang Da Mi,

286
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:34,030
instead of just standing there
with your head down,

287
00:16:34,330 --> 00:16:39,000
call the courier back and ask.
Ask exactly where he left it.

288
00:16:39,970 --> 00:16:42,710
Yes. I'll go check again.

289
00:16:50,410 --> 00:16:51,780
I praise her a little,

290
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:53,780
and she makes
such an absurd mistake.

291
00:17:04,700 --> 00:17:06,300
Please answer.

292
00:17:07,260 --> 00:17:09,830
Please pick up the phone, sir.

293
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:11,570
The number you've dialed
is unavailable.

294
00:17:11,570 --> 00:17:12,900
Please leave a message
after the tone...

295
00:17:17,410 --> 00:17:18,410
Why...

296
00:17:19,380 --> 00:17:20,540
Why aren't you answering?

297
00:17:20,540 --> 00:17:24,280
All you have to do
is tell me where you left it.

298
00:17:26,780 --> 00:17:28,820
The number you've dialed
is unavailable.

299
00:17:47,740 --> 00:17:48,770
What happened?

300
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:50,440
Why are you empty-handed?

301
00:17:50,740 --> 00:17:52,240
He's still not picking up.

302
00:17:54,580 --> 00:17:55,710
I'll try again.

303
00:17:56,310 --> 00:17:57,880
I'll go take a look,
Head Designer Cha.

304
00:17:58,880 --> 00:18:01,080
- Would you?
- It will probably be faster...

305
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,220
if I look for it.

306
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:04,890
If we keep waiting around
for Kang Da Mi,

307
00:18:04,890 --> 00:18:06,190
it could lead to disaster.

308
00:18:17,230 --> 00:18:18,870
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

309
00:18:37,090 --> 00:18:38,890
- What is it?
- What should we do, Seung Yun?

310
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:40,820
We might have to consider
the sample...

311
00:18:40,890 --> 00:18:42,230
Kang Da Mi was supposed to get...

312
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:43,830
officially lost.

313
00:18:49,730 --> 00:18:51,370
Let us wait just three more minutes
before deciding.

314
00:19:00,780 --> 00:19:03,050
I found it. This is it, right?

315
00:19:03,510 --> 00:19:04,720
(Hwanggeum Apparel, Kang Da Mi)

316
00:19:06,250 --> 00:19:08,390
That's right. That is the sample
I was supposed to pick up.

317
00:19:08,450 --> 00:19:10,250
Where did you find it,
Assistant Manager Kang?

318
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:12,790
You know that delivery drop-off spot
behind the lobby?

319
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:16,490
- It was right there.
- I definitely checked there.

320
00:19:16,960 --> 00:19:18,730
I looked everywhere,
and it was not there.

321
00:19:19,030 --> 00:19:20,560
Are you sure you looked
all the way in the back?

322
00:19:20,630 --> 00:19:22,070
Maybe you missed it...

323
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:23,270
because it was mixed
with other packages?

324
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:24,540
No...

325
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:27,840
Who found the missing sample?

326
00:19:29,470 --> 00:19:30,810
Did you find it,
Assistant Manager Kang?

327
00:19:31,480 --> 00:19:32,510
Yes, ma'am.

328
00:19:34,780 --> 00:19:35,780
Good work.

329
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:37,810
Thanks to you, we can start on time.

330
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:39,580
It was nothing, ma'am.

331
00:19:40,950 --> 00:19:42,120
Thank you, Assistant Manager Kang.

332
00:19:42,690 --> 00:19:44,690
I had so much on my mind
that I let my guard down.

333
00:19:44,760 --> 00:19:45,760
I really appreciate it.

334
00:19:49,630 --> 00:19:51,830
Are you just going to stand there
with your hands in your pockets?

335
00:19:52,100 --> 00:19:53,500
Do you need me to set up
the samples for you, too?

336
00:19:54,130 --> 00:19:56,000
No, I will do it.

337
00:20:14,550 --> 00:20:15,550
Are you all right?

338
00:20:16,990 --> 00:20:18,460
I am so glad we found it.

339
00:20:19,060 --> 00:20:20,360
That was truly terrifying.

340
00:20:21,830 --> 00:20:24,430
Every assistant
makes a mistake like that once.

341
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:26,230
Do not get discouraged.

342
00:20:27,030 --> 00:20:28,170
Thank you.

343
00:20:38,340 --> 00:20:41,350
(Conference Room)

344
00:20:43,810 --> 00:20:44,980
Head Designer Cha.

345
00:20:45,750 --> 00:20:47,550
Today's review went really well.

346
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:49,790
The concept of staying true
to the basics...

347
00:20:50,290 --> 00:20:51,690
was particularly impressive.

348
00:20:52,060 --> 00:20:53,060
Thank you.

349
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:55,290
Keep up the good work.

350
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:04,430
Kang Da Mi.

351
00:21:05,140 --> 00:21:06,800
Do you intend
to keep working like this?

352
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:09,740
I am sorry. Next time, I will...

353
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:11,810
What if Assistant Manager Kang
had not found it?

354
00:21:12,080 --> 00:21:13,480
Were we supposed to bring
the executives together,

355
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:15,380
people whose schedules
are planned to the minute,

356
00:21:15,450 --> 00:21:16,450
and just send them away?

357
00:21:17,210 --> 00:21:18,220
No, sir.

358
00:21:18,280 --> 00:21:21,890
- That should never happen.
- It almost did,

359
00:21:21,890 --> 00:21:23,050
because of you.

360
00:21:23,650 --> 00:21:26,090
Picking up a package
addressed to you from the courier...

361
00:21:26,090 --> 00:21:28,030
and bringing it here
properly on time.

362
00:21:28,630 --> 00:21:30,160
Is that one simple task
really so difficult?

363
00:21:32,100 --> 00:21:34,000
I looked everywhere,

364
00:21:35,270 --> 00:21:36,830
I thoroughly searched,

365
00:21:37,930 --> 00:21:39,540
and it really was not there,
Head Designer Cha.

366
00:21:41,140 --> 00:21:43,310
Then where did Assistant Manager Kang
find that sample?

367
00:21:44,240 --> 00:21:45,580
Did she print a new one
from the factory?

368
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:49,650
Head Designer Cha,
the issue has been resolved,

369
00:21:49,650 --> 00:21:51,180
so do you really need
to go that far?

370
00:21:51,950 --> 00:21:54,020
I am sure Kang Da Mi understood.

371
00:21:57,390 --> 00:21:59,060
She is my assistant,
Team Leader Cha.

372
00:22:00,490 --> 00:22:02,130
I know that, but still...

373
00:22:03,260 --> 00:22:05,000
Is this how you usually do your job?

374
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:09,170
I am holding my assistant accountable
for her mistake.

375
00:22:09,700 --> 00:22:11,840
Do you think it is appropriate
for you to butt in right now?

376
00:22:13,170 --> 00:22:14,200
Brother.

377
00:22:15,540 --> 00:22:16,540
"Brother?"

378
00:22:17,440 --> 00:22:19,210
We are at work,
Team Leader Cha Do Yun.

379
00:22:26,150 --> 00:22:28,250
I apologize. I will take my leave.

380
00:22:32,890 --> 00:22:35,590
I will be more careful
going forward.

381
00:22:36,330 --> 00:22:38,400
I will make sure
not to make the same mistake twice.

382
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,400
I am going to get some fresh air,

383
00:22:41,030 --> 00:22:42,170
so head to the office first...

384
00:22:42,170 --> 00:22:43,730
and write
today's collection review report.

385
00:22:44,370 --> 00:22:48,870
And if you don't know something,
please just ask right away, okay?

386
00:22:58,050 --> 00:22:59,220
You see, Assistant Manager Kang,

387
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,150
no matter how long I had to wait...

388
00:23:03,220 --> 00:23:06,660
or how much money I paid
for my luxury jewelry,

389
00:23:09,660 --> 00:23:11,360
when someone
who doesn't know their place...

390
00:23:11,430 --> 00:23:14,200
gossips or shows an interest
in what's mine...

391
00:23:16,070 --> 00:23:18,240
What happens then, ma'am?

392
00:23:18,700 --> 00:23:20,440
I absolutely hate it.

393
00:23:22,210 --> 00:23:23,710
And when I feel that way,

394
00:23:25,380 --> 00:23:27,440
I just want to get that person...

395
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:28,580
out of my sight
by any means necessary.

396
00:23:33,480 --> 00:23:34,850
You hid the sample, didn't you?

397
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:36,750
Pardon?

398
00:23:38,190 --> 00:23:40,260
Yes. But how do you know that?

399
00:23:42,360 --> 00:23:45,530
I was just on my way
to your office to tell you.

400
00:23:47,500 --> 00:23:48,500
Good work.

401
00:23:49,300 --> 00:23:52,740
Still, merely hiding a sample...

402
00:23:52,900 --> 00:23:55,070
won't be enough
to get rid of her cleanly, will it?

403
00:23:57,110 --> 00:23:58,340
Understood, ma'am.

404
00:24:11,520 --> 00:24:12,520
Honey.

405
00:24:13,860 --> 00:24:16,830
About my mother doing
a background check on you...

406
00:24:18,830 --> 00:24:21,400
I told her
that I felt hurt by that...

407
00:24:21,700 --> 00:24:23,930
and that she shouldn't do it again.

408
00:24:24,470 --> 00:24:25,540
It is all right.

409
00:24:26,370 --> 00:24:28,870
I don't mind her looking
into my background.

410
00:24:30,010 --> 00:24:32,140
What really breaks my heart is...

411
00:24:34,640 --> 00:24:35,950
Do Yun and Seung Yun.

412
00:24:37,210 --> 00:24:39,250
Your mother
treats the two boys differently.

413
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:41,590
You notice it too, don't you?

414
00:24:42,620 --> 00:24:45,590
Yesterday,
when they came back together,

415
00:24:45,790 --> 00:24:47,120
she only cared for Seung Yun.

416
00:24:47,890 --> 00:24:49,090
You saw it yourself.

417
00:24:49,860 --> 00:24:51,530
Do Yun says he is fine,

418
00:24:53,030 --> 00:24:55,130
but a mother sees
right through that.

419
00:24:58,030 --> 00:25:01,370
True. Ever since he was young,
he never showed how he felt.

420
00:25:02,970 --> 00:25:04,810
When your brother was alive,

421
00:25:05,610 --> 00:25:08,380
you were the exact same way.
You always said you were fine, too.

422
00:25:10,450 --> 00:25:12,450
Well, he was the older brother,
the firstborn,

423
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:16,120
so he meant that much more
to Mother.

424
00:25:17,420 --> 00:25:19,260
Aren't you her son, too?

425
00:25:24,130 --> 00:25:27,460
No matter how devoted I was,

426
00:25:28,900 --> 00:25:30,000
I could never replace my brother...

427
00:25:31,200 --> 00:25:32,840
in Mother's heart.

428
00:25:35,140 --> 00:25:36,170
Right.

429
00:25:36,740 --> 00:25:39,340
I thought I was
always the inadequate son to her.

430
00:25:39,810 --> 00:25:43,180
I felt like I could never surpass
my dead brother.

431
00:25:45,280 --> 00:25:46,280
I know.

432
00:25:46,550 --> 00:25:48,820
You've lived with that feeling
for a long time.

433
00:25:50,990 --> 00:25:52,390
Still, we shouldn't make Do Yun...

434
00:25:52,990 --> 00:25:55,090
feel that same way...

435
00:25:55,590 --> 00:25:57,530
you've felt your whole life,
should we?

436
00:25:59,160 --> 00:26:01,260
"No matter how hard I try,
I can't move up."

437
00:26:02,030 --> 00:26:05,000
"I will never be acknowledged
by the head of the family."

438
00:26:06,140 --> 00:26:07,670
That sense of limitation
and deprivation.

439
00:26:08,910 --> 00:26:12,240
I don't want Do Yun
to feel that way anymore.

440
00:26:18,750 --> 00:26:21,550
Shall we grab something good to eat
before heading home?

441
00:26:22,150 --> 00:26:23,390
What are you in the mood for, honey?

442
00:26:31,530 --> 00:26:32,560
Right.

443
00:26:33,560 --> 00:26:34,730
Da Mi isn't here.

444
00:26:42,710 --> 00:26:44,670
I wonder if she's eating well.

445
00:26:45,780 --> 00:26:50,750
- Grandma, I want kimchi pancakes.
- All right, sweetheart.

446
00:26:51,350 --> 00:26:52,620
Grandma will make some right away.

447
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:54,220
You're the best, Grandma.

448
00:26:54,420 --> 00:26:57,020
That yellow dress
is really pretty, Grandma.

449
00:26:57,320 --> 00:27:00,760
When you wear that dress,
you really look like a sunflower.

450
00:27:01,060 --> 00:27:02,130
A sunflower?

451
00:27:03,090 --> 00:27:04,090
Really?

452
00:27:05,060 --> 00:27:07,730
You're the best, Su Ah. Thank you.

453
00:27:08,970 --> 00:27:10,300
I should take the kimchi out first.

454
00:27:21,010 --> 00:27:23,080
Grandma, what's wrong?
Does your stomach hurt?

455
00:27:24,350 --> 00:27:26,980
No, Su Ah. I'm okay.

456
00:27:28,620 --> 00:27:30,550
Why is it acting up
all of a sudden again?

457
00:27:31,050 --> 00:27:32,290
Grandma.

458
00:27:44,800 --> 00:27:46,000
Da Mi.

459
00:27:52,340 --> 00:27:53,580
Grandma.

460
00:28:06,490 --> 00:28:08,360
(Mission: Mompossible)

461
00:28:08,560 --> 00:28:10,460
Mother, I'm going inside now.

462
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:14,700
- I heard you can't even eat.
- I've lived for far too long.

463
00:28:14,830 --> 00:28:19,200
- Is this Jo Mi Mi?
- Kang Dae Chi, come down here.

464
00:28:19,370 --> 00:28:20,940
I'm calling because
the doctor found something...

465
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:22,270
that requires further examination.

466
00:28:22,310 --> 00:28:23,310
They told me to come in,

467
00:28:23,310 --> 00:28:24,470
saying they can't discuss it
over the phone.

468
00:28:24,540 --> 00:28:26,310
Does that mean it's really bad?

469
00:28:29,510 --> 00:28:31,510
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
